            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court held that the six\u2011year statute of limitations for an APA claim begins when the plaintiff has the right to apply to the court for relief, i.e., when the plaintiff is injured by the final agency action."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "623b36ce767f3ecb639d9bae6e989e405892ff64ced272f19c3266b1a5df2c21",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-623b36ce767f-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court reversed the Eighth Circuit\u2019s judgment and remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "623b36ce767f3ecb639d9bae6e989e405892ff64ced272f19c3266b1a5df2c21",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-623b36ce767f-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 29,
              "start": 29
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kavanaugh, in a concurring opinion, agreed that an APA claim accrues when the plaintiff is injured by the challenged agency rule."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "623b36ce767f3ecb639d9bae6e989e405892ff64ced272f19c3266b1a5df2c21",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-623b36ce767f-0004-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Jackson dissented, arguing that vacatur is an appropriate remedy when a federal court finds an agency rule unlawful, and that Corner Post could obtain meaningful relief through vacatur."
      }
    ],
